"""DSB-41 <- LATCH case travel-realistic-family-trip-002 (hard five-person
Chicago->Seattle family trip). Progressive disclosure, noisy flight and hotel
inventory, a provider-confirmed held room whose rate goes over cap and whose
hold lapses, a mid-window flight cancellation, and one exact-plan approval gate
in front of both bookings.

Fold of the case's 23 all-$ref tools into the DSB surface (behavior is
indistinguishable wherever folded; each fold is noted):
  user.dialogue          -> hidden kind="dialogue" tool trip_dialogue (kept)
  transport.compare      -> hidden catalog transport_modes (kept)
  flight.search          -> hidden catalog flight_search (kept)
  flight.compare         -> folded into flight_search: the codeshare trap lives
                            in the rows (physical_flight_key + operating flight
                            numbers), a re-query is the comparison
  flight.refresh         -> folded into flight_search: catalog updates and
                            per-row expires_at make re-querying the refresh
  flight.select          -> folded into the one-shot select tool book_flight
  hotel.search           -> hidden catalog hotel_search (kept)
  hotel.select           -> folded into the one-shot select tool book_hotel
  hotel.refresh          -> folded into hotel_search (same as flight.refresh)
  provider.contact       -> DSB mail: send_email to the Lakefront accessibility
                            desk (lakefront_desk); the rule-based workflow is
                            the evt-provider-htl-301-confirmed provider.reply
  provider.inbox         -> DSB read_inbox: the desk reply carries the written
                            accessibility verification evidence
  route.search           -> hidden catalog access_routes (kept)
  route.verify           -> folded into access_routes: verified rows issue the
                            route evidence on retrieval (the CityStep desk can
                            also re-confirm by mail)
  dining.search          -> hidden catalog dining_search (kept)
  dining.verify          -> folded into dining_search: confirmed rows issue the
                            shellfish-protocol evidence on retrieval
  attraction.search      -> hidden catalog attraction_search (kept)
  itinerary.build        -> folded into the trip_plans catalog plus the
  budget.calculate          confirm_trip_plan select: plan rows carry the exact
  plan.present              itinerary, category totals and the complete budget,
                            and the select records the approved plan
  approval.record        -> folded into confirm_trip_plan (the plan_approved
                            fact) plus the dialogue approval rule; DSB has no
                            separate approval apparatus (dsb13/dsb17 precedent)
  booking.create         -> the two select tools book_flight and book_hotel
  booking.status         -> the {"query": ...} readback of those select tools
  time.wait              -> the common wait_until tool

Adaptations (documented deviations from the authored case):
  - Deadline kept (2027-05-20T18:00, a 19.4-day window, >= the 2-day DSB
    minimum), so no deadline move was needed.
  - Event times: the provider reply at 2027-05-03T03:00 becomes the
    htl-301-confirmed row's available_at 2027-05-03T08:00 plus the desk's mail
    reply landing the same morning (business-hours coherence).
  - The 05-10 flight cancellation also removes the AC-9417 codeshare row: it is
    the same physical flight (SB|417|2027-06-12|08:20), so keeping it "available"
    after the cancellation would be incoherent; this sharpens the V2 dedup trap.
  - Itinerary: the case's expected itinerary used att-603/att-604, whose only
    routes from htl-302 violate the accessibility policy (route-403 stale,
    route-404 0.6 miles) - an authoring inconsistency. The recovered plan uses
    the two attractions with compliant current verified routes (Space Needle
    via CS-SEA-01, Great Wheel via CS-SEA-06), one per day, with hotel rest
    afternoons on June 14 and 15; the budget is recomputed accordingly
    (5615 USD: 2390 + 1680 + 360 + 620 + 265 + 300, all within caps).
  - din-508 (child_menu false) is dropped from the required dining set - the
    rubric's own R4 requires a child menu for family dinners; it stays as a
    catalog decoy.
  - Morgan's approval window (May 12 at 12:00 Chicago time) is authored so the
    two inventory events (May 10 flight cancellation, May 12 hotel rate change)
    land before any disciplined booking; DSB select desks are one-shot, so
    booking the invalidated favourites early burns the desk - the ported form of
    LATCH's booking-before-approval hard violation.
  - hold_expired: the Lakefront hold desk (place_hotel_hold) is a select tool
    with hold_minutes; DSB has no hold->booking conversion operation, so an
    unconverted hold always lapses (status "expired" frees the desk), which the
    reference crosses as the fourth event. The provider's own hold expiry is
    additionally announced by the May 14 page update.
"""

